    "updated_at": "2021-02-02T08:16:51Z",
    "body": "I've just had a look at the change. It seems that the issue itself is independent of using `process_control` and the timeout, but can be triggered by simply changing `utils::internal_exec_cmd()` to use `std::process` differently.\r\n\r\nBefore the commit above the code was using [std::process::Command.output()](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/struct.Command.html#method.output) to execute the command and capture its output.\r\n\r\nSimply changing the code to [spawn()](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/struct.Command.html#method.spawn) the process and then use the resulting `Child` object's [wait_with_output()](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/struct.Child.html#method.wait_with_output) method triggers the issue (without introducing 3rd party dependencies).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
