    "body": "@davidkna No, it doesn't seem to help.\r\n\r\nBased on the stdlib source it seems to me that the only difference between calling `output()` and `spawn()` is that `output()` calls the internal spawn implementation like [this](https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/process.rs.html#876-881):\r\n\r\n```\r\nspawn(imp::Stdio::MakePipe, false)\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhile `spawn()` calls it like [this](https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/process.rs.html#847-849):\r\n\r\n```\r\nspawn(imp::Stdio::Inherit, true)\r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
